===== 9.0.0~dev =====
* Module namespace modernization
** Public modules are now accessed as Os.Session, Os.User, Os.Tips,
   Os.Email, Os.Notif, ... instead of the legacy flat Os_xxx prefix.
** New ocsigen-start-compat opam package: provides the legacy
   Os_xxx module names as include-aliases of the new Os.Xxx
   modules, to ease migration of existing code.
* PROJECT_NAME_icons.eliom in the distillery template is now
  parameterised on Eliom.Content.Html.T (the shared signature
  exposed by Eliom 13) instead of an ad-hoc ICON_HTML signature.
* Os.Page: the error pages are sent with an HTTP status matching the error:
  403 when the user may not see the page (Session.Not_connected,
  Session.Permission_denied, a predicate returning false), 404 when what it
  shows does not exist (Eliom.Common.Eliom_404, User.No_such_user,
  Db.No_such_user, Db.No_such_resource, Handlers.No_such_resource), 500 for
  any other exception, Not_found included, as in Eliom. They used to be
  sent with 200. The fallback may set another one with
  Eliom.Registration.set_status (Eliom 13).
* Os.Session also puts the service session in the group of the user, as
  it already did for the data sessions: at login, when the session is
  restored, and when the service session has left the group. Services
  registered with scope Eliom.Common.default_group_scope are now shared
  by all the sessions of the user (Eliom 13), and
  Os.Session.disconnect_all closes them. A service session, with its
  cookie, is now created at login.
* Distillery template
** Renamed from os.pgocaml to os.
** Unknown URLs get a page of the application, with status 404, through
   Eliom.Registration.set_exn_handler, instead of the default error page
   of Ocsigen Server. Eliom then answers these URLs itself: extensions
   placed after <eliom/> in the configuration no longer see them, and
   each unknown URL costs a full page of the application, session
   included.
** Database schema: the tables of Ocsigen Start are now in
   ocsigen_start.sql, a replayable file copied into the project,
   which creates them on a new database and brings them up to date
   from any release since 0.99. Its trigger functions live in the
   schema ocsigen_start; the helper trigger_exists of the previous
   templates is dropped. PROJECT_NAME.sql only holds the schema of
   the application, and is replayable too. make db-update applies
   both; it replaces db-schema and the dead db-upgrade target.
   db-create also creates the Ocsipersist database.
   To move an existing project to this layout: copy
   ocsigen_start.sql from the new template; take db-update and
   OS_PSQL_FILE from its Makefile.db and Makefile.options; remove
   the Ocsigen Start part from PROJECT_NAME.sql and make the rest
   replayable, as the header of the new PROJECT_NAME.sql explains;
   then run make db-update.
** The set_main_email trigger of the template schema now names the
   users table with its schema: adding an email to a user created
   without one failed with the default search_path.
** Source directory renamed back to template.distillery/ (the
   convention used by ocsigen-start's previous Makefile-based
   build), and now installed via dune
   (install (section lib_root) (files (glob_files_rec
   (template.distillery/{*,.*} with_prefix eliom/templates/os))))
   so the template lands at lib/eliom/templates/os/, where
   eliom-distillery picks it up at the standard location (Eliom
   13 dropped the per-package eliom-templates/ auto-discovery).
** template.distillery is now generated from the os_template
   repository by script/update_template.sh.
** No data directory in the configuration: Ocsipersist gets its
   location from <database> or <store>.
** New demo page for forms, with a button to show the password.
   Style update.
** New layout: the code of the application is a library in lib/,
   its entry module is in app/, and app/main/ is an executable that
   links Ocsigen Server as a library (make test.static.byte). Their
   dune rules are generated by ocsigen-dune-rules.
** The WASM client is enabled with USE_WASM, both in the
   configuration file and in the executable.
* Migrated to the new Eliom 13 module names (Eliom.Service,
  Eliom.Content, Eliom.Common, ...) and to the wrapped
  ocsigenserver module names (Ocsigen.Server, Ocsigen.Extensions,
  Ocsigen.Config, Ocsigen_base.Lib, ...).
* The library is built with dune and ocsigen-dune-rules instead of
  Makefiles.
* Dependencies: OCaml >= 5.1, Eliom 13, Ocsigen Toolkit 5,
  ocsigen-i18n 6, ocsigen-ppx-rpc 2, ocsipersist-pgsql-config 3.1,
  js_of_ocaml >= 6.4. conf-postgresql replaces the depexts on
  PostgreSQL.
* Documentation: the API documentation and the manual are written
  with odoc, and published on ocsigen.org and ocaml.org.
* Os.Email: the default email-sending function now pipes an RFC-2822
  message to the configured mailer ("sendmail" by default) via
  Lwt_process, instead of printing to stdout. If the mailer is not on
  PATH, the email is logged to stderr so the application stays usable
  out of the box. The now-unused [Invalid_mailer] exception is removed.
* Os.Services: the services of phone connectivity are marked with
  Eliom.Service.allow_unregistered, so that Eliom 13 does not warn about
  them when an application does not enable phone connectivity.

===== 8.0.0 (2026-02) =====
* Compatibility with Eliom 12, js_of_ocaml 6.3, OCaml 5.3 and 5.4
* Logging with Logs instead of Lwt_log
* Template: loads the WASM client in browsers that support it
* Os_page.other_head is now a function, so that the template can
  insert the script that chooses between JavaScript and WASM
* ocsipersist-pgsql-config is a dependency of ocsigen-start
* The library no longer uses lwt_ppx

===== 7.1.0 (2024-11) =====
* Compatibility with WASM

===== 7.0.0 (2024-09) =====
* Compatibility with Ocsigen Server 6
* Build an app as an executable, with Ocsigen Server as a library, without config file

===== 6.3.0 (2024-03-25) =====
* Adding license Unlicense to the template
* Dependecy to Tyxml >= 4.6

===== 6.2.0 (2024-02-18) =====
* Template simplification

===== 6.1.0 (2022-03-08) =====
* Adjust the server-side interface of Os_session.disconnect_all

===== 4.0.0 (2021-01-13) =====
